 = Σ_industries ( donorShare(industry) × billWeight(industry) ), where billWeight = classifierConfidence / Σ classifierConfidence. Range 0–1, read as a weighted share of disclosed itemized money.","donorProfileCycle":2026,"billClassificationMethod":"llm","unclassifiedDonorShare":0.7526003778846865},"bill":{"id":"119-hjres-54","congress":119,"billType":"hjres","billNumber":"54","title":"Proposing an amendment to the Constitution of the United States providing that the rights protected and extended by the Constitution are the rights of natural persons only.","introducedDate":"2025-02-12","latestActionDate":"2025-02-12","latestActionText":"Referred to the House Committee on the Judiciary.","policyArea":"Civil Rights and Liberties, Minority Issues","subjects":["Constitution and constitutional amendments","Elections, voting, political campaign regulation","First Amendment rights"],"sponsorBioguideId":"J000298","cosponsorCount":77,"committeeNames":[],"congressDotGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-joint-resolution/54","industries":[{"industry":"finance-banking","confidence":0.85,"rationale":"The amendment would subject banks and financial firms to new constitutional limits on political spending and strip them of constitutional rights currently recognized for corporations."},{"industry":"tech","confidence":0.85,"rationale":"Technology companies would lose constitutional protections as corporate entities and face new restrictions on election-related expenditures and contributions."},{"industry":"energy-fossil","confidence":0.8,"rationale":"Oil, gas, and coal companies would be subject to campaign finance limits and lose constitutional rights currently available to corporate entities."},{"industry":"pharma","confidence":0.8,"rationale":"Pharmaceutical and device manufacturers would face new restrictions on political spending and lose constitutional protections as artificial entities."},{"industry":"legal","confidence":0.75,"rationale":"Law firms and lobbying organizations would operate under new campaign finance regulations and potentially altered constitutional frameworks for corporate clients."},{"industry":"media-entertainment","confidence":0.7,"rationale":"Media corporations would lose constitutional rights as artificial entities, potentially affecting their ability to make election-related expenditures and editorial decisions."}],"plainSummary":"This proposed constitutional amendment would establish that only individual human beings—not corporations or other artificial entities—hold rights under the Constitution. It would require all levels of government to regulate or limit campaign contributions and spending, including candidates' own funds, to ensure equal political access regardless of wealth. The amendment would also mandate public disclosure of all permitted contributions and prevent courts from treating campaign spending as protected speech under the First Amendment.","classificationMethod":"llm","plain":{"whoItTouches":"Anyone who votes.","confidence":"crs-summary"},"topOverlap":{"bioguideId":"W000788","score":0.04129443420932792},"overlapCount":75},"meaning":{"percentile":36.867013724562234,"median":0.01073720309570498,"n":6339,"ordinary":[{"kind":"state-industry","text":"Banking & Finance is also the top donor sector for 4 other members from OH. That points to the industry being big in the state, not to anything about this member."}],"unattributedShare":0.7526003778846865}},{"billId":"119-hres-1286","bioguideId":"K000009","cycle":2026,"score":0.0035790392190981476,"matches":[{"industry":"transport","donorAmount":15500,"donorShare":0.005426912728958604,"billConfidence":0.4,"contribution":0.002411961212870491},{"industry":"manufacturing","donorAmount":6000,"donorShare":0.002100740411209782,"billConfidence":0.5,"contribution":0.0011670780062276568}],"method":{"formula":"score = Σ_industries ( donorShare(industry) × billWeight(industry) ), where billWeight = classifierConfidence / Σ classifierConfiden